To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Rhode Island Access to Public Records Act, I hereby request the following records:

**APRA Request — Five-Year History of Public-Records Fee Estimates and Charges**

To the APRA Records Officer:

Pursuant to the Rhode Island Access to Public Records Act, R.I. Gen. Laws § 38-2-1 et seq., I request the records described below for the period of **September 14, 2021 through September 14, 2026**.

**The specific purpose of this request is to understand, verify, and evaluate how the Scituate Police Department calculated and justified the $438.75 estimate that I was required to pay in connection with my currently pending APRA request.**

I am requesting the Department's historical APRA estimates and charges so that I can compare the methodology used in my request against the Department's actual historical practices involving similar requests. Specifically, I want to determine whether the time, rates, redaction expenses, processing costs, and overall methodology used to calculate my $438.75 charge are consistent with what the Department has charged other members of the public for comparable records.

Accordingly, I request:

1. Any APRA request log, spreadsheet, database, index, tracking document, or other existing record identifying APRA requests received by the Scituate Police Department during this five-year period, including, where maintained:

* Date received;
* Request or tracking number;
* General subject and scope;
* Type of records requested;
* Date completed;
* Estimated processing time;
* Estimated cost;
* Final amount charged or collected;
* Whether a fee was reduced, waived, refunded, or not collected.

2. Copies of all written **cost estimates, deposit requests, invoices, fee calculations, worksheets, and itemizations** issued in connection with APRA requests during this period.

3. Records sufficient to identify the general nature and scope of the request associated with each estimate so that the estimates can be meaningfully compared. I do not need the private personal information of previous requesters.

4. Existing records showing how APRA estimates and charges were calculated, including:

* Estimated and actual employee hours;
* Hourly rates;
* Search and retrieval time;
* Review and redaction time;
* Number and type of records involved;
* Video or audio duration;
* Electronic-production charges;
* Outside-vendor charges;
* Vendor quotes or invoices;
* Application of any free search-and-retrieval time required by law.

5. Records concerning APRA requests involving **body-worn-camera footage, cruiser or dash-camera footage, dispatch audio, surveillance video, photographs, or other police audio/video evidence**, together with the estimates and final charges associated with those requests.

6. Records showing instances in which an APRA estimate was reduced, modified, waived, refunded, or where records were ultimately provided without charge after an estimate had initially been issued.

7. All policies, procedures, fee schedules, calculation methods, written instructions, guidance, or training materials used by the Department to determine APRA charges.

8. All records specifically supporting the calculation of the **$438.75 estimate charged to me**, including any worksheet, calculation, time estimate, anticipated redaction time, number or duration of recordings, employee time, vendor cost, hourly rate, or other information relied upon to arrive at that amount.

9. All records sufficient to explain and substantiate the amount of **redaction time included in the $438.75 estimate**, particularly in light of any automated, AI-assisted, or software-based redaction capabilities available through Axon or any other system used by the Department.

This specifically includes:

* The number of hours attributed to reviewing and redacting the requested body-camera footage;
* A breakdown of what specific tasks allegedly require that amount of employee or vendor time;
* Identification of the software or system used to review and redact body-camera footage;
* Whether that software provides automated or AI-assisted detection, tracking, blurring, muting, or other redaction functions;
* Records showing whether automated redaction tools were considered or used when calculating my estimate;
* Any policies, training materials, manuals, vendor documentation, or written guidance concerning automated or AI-assisted redaction capabilities;
* An explanation, supported by existing records, of why the estimated redaction process requires the amount of manual labor charged to me if automated redaction technology is available; and
* Records showing how the Department calculated redaction time for comparable body-camera requests during the preceding five years.

The purpose of this portion of my request is to determine whether the substantial redaction time incorporated into my **$438.75 estimate is actually supported by the work reasonably necessary to process the footage**, and whether that estimate is consistent with the technology available to the Department and with the manner in which comparable requests have historically been processed and charged.

Again, **the purpose of this request is to determine whether the $438.75 estimate imposed upon my request is consistent with the Scituate Police Department's historical charges and established methodology for comparable APRA requests.**

This request seeks the records necessary to independently verify how that amount was calculated and whether the same standards have been consistently applied to other public-records requesters.

This is a **separate APRA request** and does not modify, supplement, expand, replace, delay, suspend, or restart the response period for my existing request for which the Department has already accepted payment of **$438.75**.

Before incurring any charge exceeding **$25 for this new request**, please provide a detailed written estimate explaining the anticipated work and calculation. No charges exceeding that amount are authorized without my prior written approval.

Please provide responsive records electronically and in native format where reasonably available. If any responsive record is withheld or redacted, please identify the applicable statutory exemption and produce all reasonably segregable non-exempt portions.

Please confirm receipt.

Thank you,

**Joshua Grissom**

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 10 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Josh Grissom
